the generate-then-search pattern that terminated Cycles 001–010.

## 4. Methodological Shift from Cycle 010
- Cycles 001–010: GENERATE → SEARCH → CLEARANCE (post-hoc destruction).
- Cycle 011: CLEARANCE CONSTRAINTS → REGISTRY-FIRST FILTER → CONTROLLED
  GENERATION (10 candidates max) → IMMEDIATE DESTRUCTION → PROFESSIONAL HANDOFF.
- Track A (acquisition/existing-asset scout) run in parallel with Track B
  (clearance-constrained new-name generation).

## 5. Historical Learning Applied (from Cycle 010 §2)
1. Vowel-final coined families → excluded.
2. Hard-consonant tails (-ant/-ent/-ith/-ast/-ont) → excluded.
3. Two-word neutral semantic pairs → excluded.
4. "Search-sparse ≠ available" → registry-first, not search-first.
5. Fantasy/fan-wiki morphology → excluded.
6. Personal-name shapes (Slavic -ov/-ski, Nordic -sen) → excluded.
7. Public aftermarket surfaces insufficient → Track A ceiling explicitly recognized.
8. Trademark clearance the largest gap → REQUIRES PROFESSIONAL CLEARANCE labelling
   used throughout.
9. Volume is not the solution → n=10 hard cap enforced.
Rejected names not recycled: PALVEDRANT, Quenlox, Axenomik, Qrivax, Belrast,
Halront, Kelvant, Bordith.

