## 22. Strategic Learning
1. Registry-first upstream constraint mapping does NOT by itself remove
   the surname / pharma / active-company collision space for short (6–10
   letter) coined marks under public-web evidence.
2. The persistent binding constraint remains AUTHORITATIVE REGISTRY /
   PROFESSIONAL CLEARANCE ACCESS — not creative morphology.
3. Track A (public acquisition surfaces without paid brokerage) remains
   informationally insufficient for asset acquisition.
4. The Cycle 001–010 → 011 pattern demonstrates the naming problem is
   ACCESS-BOUND, not CREATIVITY-BOUND. Further generative cycles at the
   same access level will reproduce the same terminal state.

## 23. Next-Cycle Trigger (per §19)
Do NOT run Cycle 012 as another broad creative naming cycle. Trigger one
or more of:
1. IP counsel engagement (ID and/or US/EU) with authoritative DJKI/PDKI,
   USPTO, EUIPO, WIPO access.
2. Paid brokerage / off-market acquisition search for existing brand
   assets.
3. Deliberate naming pause under a working codename; ship product;
   revisit brand only after professional access is procured.

